From: lwj <lw91411@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: sfp: add quirk for OEM SFP+XG-T-H 2.5G copper module

The OEM SFP+XG-T-H is a 2.5G copper module which does not perform clause 37
negotiation on the host side, but it does claim the Autoneg link mode in its
supported link modes.

phylink therefore selects the in-band AN path (PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED)
for the 2500BASE-X link, and phylink_decode_c37_word() only reports the link
as being up once the link partner advertises 2500baseX/Full in its C37 word.
As this module never sends a C37 word, the link is reported as down forever
even though the module itself is linked -- on the BPI-R4 Pro 4E the MxL862xx
XPCS reports the link in its PCS state ("Main state: link_up" in
/sys/kernel/debug/sfp1/state), but sfp-lan stays in NO-CARRIER.

Clear the Autoneg bit so that the out-of-band path is used instead:
phylink_mii_c22_pcs_decode_state() then derives speed and duplex from the
interface when the PCS reports the link as up, and phylink calls
pcs_link_up(2500, FULL), which makes the MxL862xx firmware bring the link up.

Signed-off-by: lwj <lw91411@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -584,6 +584,13 @@ static const struct sfp_quirk sfp_quirks[] = {
 
 	SFP_QUIRK_F("OEM", "SFP-10G-T", sfp_fixup_rollball_cc),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-T", sfp_quirk_oem_2_5g),
+	// OEM SFP+XG-T-H is a 2.5G copper module which does not support
+	// clause 37 negotiation on the host side, but it still claims the
+	// Autoneg link mode.  phylink then enables in-band AN for 2500BASE-X
+	// and only reports the link as being up once the link partner's C37
+	// word advertises 2500baseX/Full, which never happens.  Clear the
+	// Autoneg bit so that the out-of-band path is used instead.
+	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP+XG-T-H", sfp_quirk_disable_autoneg),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-BX10-D", sfp_quirk_2500basex),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-BX10-U", sfp_quirk_2500basex),
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("OEM", "SFP-2.5G-LH03-B", sfp_quirk_2500basex),
